_CHOICE','Opposite = 4, Adjacent = 3, Hypotenuse = 5. sin A = 4/5.',2.00,0.50,1,'2026-10-02 13:12:41'),(1572,15,'If x + 1/x = 5, find the value of x^2 + 1/x^2:','Quantitative Aptitude & Reasoning','SINGLE_CHOICE','x^2 + 1/x^2 = (x + 1/x)^2 - 2 = 25 - 2 = 23.',2.00,0.50,2,'2026-10-02 13:12:41'),(1573,15,'Find the single equivalent discount percentage for two successive discounts of 20% and 10%:','Quantitative Aptitude & Reasoning','SINGLE_CHOICE','Equivalent discount = 20 + 10 - (20*10)/100 = 30 - 2 = 28%.',2.00,0.50,3,'2026-10-02 13:12:41'),(1574,15,'The perimeter of a circular field is 440 meters. Find its radius (Take π = 22/7):','Quantitative Aptitude & Reasoning','SINGLE_CHOICE','2 * (22/7) * r = 440 => r = (440 * 7) / 44 = 70 meters.',2.00,0.50,4,'2026-10-02 13:12:41'),(1575,15,'A can do a piece of work in 15 days and B in 20 days. If they work together for 4 days, what fraction of work is left?','Quantitative Aptitude & Reasoning','SINGLE_CHOICE','1 day work = 1/15 + 1/20 = 7/60. 4 days work = 28/60 = 7/15. Work left = 1 - 7/15 = 8/15.',2.00,0.50,5,'2026-10-02 13:12:41'),(1576,15,'In a right-angled triangle ABC right-angled at B, if tan A = 4/3, what is the value of sin A?','Quantitative Aptitude & Reasoning','SINGLE_CHOICE','Opposite = 4, Adjacent = 3, Hypotenuse = 5. sin A = 4/5.',2.00,0.50,6,'2026-10-02 13:12:41'),(1577,15,'If x + 1/x = 5, find the value of x^2 + 1/x^2:','Quantitative Aptitude & Reasoning','SINGLE_CHOICE','x^2 + 1/x^2 = (x + 1/x)^2 - 2 = 25 - 2 = 23.',2.00,0.50,7,'2026-10-02 13:12:41'),(1578,15,'Find the single equivalent discount percentage for two successive discounts of 20% and 10%:','Quantitative Aptitude & Reasoning','SINGLE_CHOICE','Equivalent discount = 20 + 10 - (20*10)/100 = 30 - 2 = 28%.',2.00,0.50,8,'2026-10-02 13:12:41'),(1579,15,'The perimeter of a circular field is 440 meters. Find its radius (Take π = 22/7):','Quantitative Aptitude & Reasoning','SINGLE_CHOICE','2 * (22/7) * r = 440 => r = (440 * 7) / 44 = 70 meters.',2.00,0.5