,'2026-10-02 13:12:41'),(2171,1,'What does CPU stand for in computer hardware?','Hardware Basics','SINGLE_CHOICE','CPU stands for Central Processing Unit.',2.00,0.50,1,'2026-10-02 17:28:37'),(2172,5,'Which keyword is used to declare a block-scoped variable in JavaScript?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','The let keyword declares a block-scoped variable whose value can be reassigned.',2.00,0.50,1,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2173,5,'Which keyword is used to declare a block-scoped constant in JavaScript?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','The const keyword creates a block-scoped binding that cannot be reassigned after initialization.',2.00,0.50,2,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2174,5,'What will typeof null return in JavaScript?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','Due to a historical behavior in JavaScript, typeof null returns \"object\".',2.00,0.50,3,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2175,5,'Which operator checks both value and data type equality in JavaScript?','Operators & Type Coercion','SINGLE_CHOICE','The strict equality operator === compares both the value and the data type without performing type coercion.',2.00,0.50,4,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2176,5,'What is the result of 5 == \'5\' in JavaScript?','Operators & Type Coercion','SINGLE_CHOICE','The == operator performs type coercion before comparison, so the number 5 and string \'5\' are considered equal.',2.00,0.50,5,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2177,5,'Which ES6 feature allows a function to be written using a shorter syntax?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Arrow functions provide a shorter syntax for writing functions and have lexical handling of this.',2.00,0.50,6,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2178,5,'Which syntax is used to create a template literal in JavaScript?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Template literals use backticks (`) and support embedded expressions using ${}.',2.00,0.50,7,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2179,5,'Which ES6 feature allows values to be extracted from arrays or objects into variables?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Destructuring assignment allows values from arrays or properties from objects to be assigned to variables conveniently.',2.00,0.50,8,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2180,5,'Which syntax is used to collect multiple function arguments into an array?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','The rest parameter syntax (...args) collects multiple arguments into an array.',2.00,0.50,9,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2181,5,'What does the spread operator (...) primarily do when used with an array?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','The spread operator expands the elements of an iterable such as an array into individual elements.',2.00,0.50,10,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2182,5,'Which ES6 feature is used to define reusable classes in JavaScript?','Classes & OOP','SINGLE_CHOICE','ES6 introduced the class syntax for defining objects and implementing object-oriented programming patterns.',2.00,0.50,11,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2183,5,'Which method is automatically called when an instance of an ES6 class is created?','Classes & OOP','SINGLE_CHOICE','The constructor() method is automatically invoked when a new instance of a class is created.',2.00,0.50,12,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2184,5,'Which keyword is used to inherit from another class in ES6?','Classes & OOP','SINGLE_CHOICE','The extends keyword creates a subclass that inherits from another class.',2.00,0.50,13,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2185,5,'Which keyword is used to call the constructor of a parent class?','Classes & OOP','SINGLE_CHOICE','The super() call invokes the parent class constructor from a derived class.',2.00,0.50,14,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2186,5,'Which ES6 feature is used to organize and reuse JavaScript code across files?','Modules','SINGLE_CHOICE','ES6 modules allow code to be separated into files and shared using export and import statements.',2.00,0.50,15,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2187,5,'Which keyword is used to make a value available for import from an ES6 module?','Modules','SINGLE_CHOICE','The export keyword makes variables, functions, classes, or other declarations available to other modules.',2.00,0.50,16,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2188,5,'Which keyword is used to load an exported value from another ES6 module?','Modules','SINGLE_CHOICE','The import keyword is used to bring exported bindings from another ES6 module into the current module.',2.00,0.50,17,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2189,5,'What does a Promise represent in JavaScript?','Asynchronous JavaScript','SINGLE_CHOICE','A Promise represents the eventual result of an asynchronous operation and can be pending, fulfilled, or rejected.',2.00,0.50,18,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2190,5,'Which keyword is used to pause execution inside an async function until a Promise settles?','Async/Await','SINGLE_CHOICE','The await keyword pauses execution within an async function until the associated Promise is fulfilled or rejected.',2.00,0.50,19,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2191,5,'Which keyword is used to declare a function that always returns a Promise?','Async/Await','SINGLE_CHOICE','An async function automatically returns a Promise and allows the use of await inside its body.',2.00,0.50,20,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2192,5,'What is a closure in JavaScript?','Functions & Closures','SINGLE_CHOICE','A closure occurs when a function retains access to variables from its lexical outer scope even after that outer function has finished executing.',2.00,0.50,21,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2193,5,'What is hoisting in JavaScript?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','Hoisting describes how JavaScript processes certain declarations before executing the surrounding code.',2.00,0.50,22,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2194,5,'Which method creates a new array containing elements that satisfy a condition?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The filter() method creates a new array containing elements for which the callback returns true.',2.00,0.50,23,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2195,5,'Which array method transforms every element and returns a new array?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The map() method applies a callback to every element and returns a new array containing the transformed values.',2.00,0.50,24,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2196,5,'Which array method is commonly used to reduce an array to a single value?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The reduce() method processes array elements and accumulates them into a single resulting value.',2.00,0.50,25,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2197,5,'Which ES6 collection stores unique values?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','A Set is a collection that stores unique values and automatically ignores duplicate entries.',2.00,0.50,26,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2198,5,'Which ES6 collection stores key-value pairs and allows keys of any value type?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','Map stores key-value pairs and allows keys to be values of different types, including objects and functions.',2.00,0.50,27,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2199,5,'Which operator provides a default value when the left-hand value is null or undefined?','Modern JavaScript','SINGLE_CHOICE','The nullish coalescing operator ?? returns the right-hand value when the left-hand value is null or undefined.',2.00,0.50,28,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2200,5,'Which operator allows safe access to a property when an object may be null or undefined?','Modern JavaScript','SINGLE_CHOICE','Optional chaining (?.) safely accesses properties or methods without throwing an error when an intermediate value is null or undefined.',2.00,0.50,29,'2026-10-03 02:40:40'),(2201,5,'Which keyword is used to declare a block-scoped variable whose value can be reassigned?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','The let keyword declares a block-scoped variable that can be reassigned.',2.00,0.50,1,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2202,5,'Which keyword is used to declare a block-scoped variable that cannot be reassigned?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','The const keyword creates a block-scoped binding that cannot be reassigned.',2.00,0.50,2,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2203,5,'Which keyword was traditionally used for function-scoped variable declarations?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','The var keyword declares variables with function scope rather than block scope.',2.00,0.50,3,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2204,5,'What does typeof null return in JavaScript?','Data Types','SINGLE_CHOICE','Due to a historical behavior in JavaScript, typeof null returns \"object\".',2.00,0.50,4,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2205,5,'Which operator performs strict equality comparison in JavaScript?','Operators','SINGLE_CHOICE','The === operator compares both value and type without performing type coercion.',2.00,0.50,5,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2206,5,'What is the result of 5 === \'5\'?','Operators','SINGLE_CHOICE','The values have different types, so strict equality returns false.',2.00,0.50,6,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2207,5,'What is the result of 5 == \'5\'?','Type Coercion','SINGLE_CHOICE','The == operator performs type coercion before comparison, making 5 and \'5\' equal.',2.00,0.50,7,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2208,5,'Which value represents the absence of an assigned value?','Data Types','SINGLE_CHOICE','undefined commonly indicates that a variable has been declared but has not been assigned a value.',2.00,0.50,8,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2209,5,'Which value represents an intentional absence of an object value?','Data Types','SINGLE_CHOICE','null is commonly used to explicitly indicate that a value is intentionally absent.',2.00,0.50,9,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2210,5,'Which ES6 feature provides a shorter syntax for writing functions?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Arrow functions provide a concise syntax for defining functions.',2.00,0.50,10,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2211,5,'Which syntax is used to create a template literal?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Template literals are enclosed in backticks and support embedded expressions.',2.00,0.50,11,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2212,5,'Which syntax is used to insert an expression inside a template literal?','Template Literals','SINGLE_CHOICE','Expressions are embedded in template literals using ${expression}.',2.00,0.50,12,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2213,5,'What is destructuring in JavaScript?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Destructuring allows values from arrays or properties from objects to be assigned directly to variables.',2.00,0.50,13,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2214,5,'Which operator is used for the spread syntax?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','The three-dot syntax (...) is used for spread and rest operations.',2.00,0.50,14,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2215,5,'What does the spread syntax do when used with an array?','Spread Operator','SINGLE_CHOICE','Spread syntax expands the elements of an iterable into individual elements.',2.00,0.50,15,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2216,5,'Which syntax collects multiple function arguments into an array?','Rest Parameters','SINGLE_CHOICE','A rest parameter such as ...args collects remaining function arguments into an array.',2.00,0.50,16,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2217,5,'Which keyword is used to define a class in ES6?','Classes','SINGLE_CHOICE','ES6 introduced the class syntax for defining classes.',2.00,0.50,17,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2218,5,'Which method is automatically called when a new class instance is created?','Classes','SINGLE_CHOICE','The constructor() method is called automatically when an object is created using new.',2.00,0.50,18,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2219,5,'Which keyword is used to inherit from another class?','Classes & Inheritance','SINGLE_CHOICE','The extends keyword is used to create a subclass of another class.',2.00,0.50,19,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2220,5,'Which keyword is used to access the parent class constructor or methods?','Classes & Inheritance','SINGLE_CHOICE','The super keyword is used to call the parent constructor or access parent methods.',2.00,0.50,20,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2221,5,'Which keyword is used to export functionality from an ES6 module?','Modules','SINGLE_CHOICE','The export keyword makes declarations available to other modules.',2.00,0.50,21,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2222,5,'Which keyword is used to import functionality from another ES6 module?','Modules','SINGLE_CHOICE','The import keyword is used to import exported bindings from another module.',2.00,0.50,22,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2223,5,'Which statement correctly imports a default export named calculate?','Modules','SINGLE_CHOICE','A default export is imported without curly braces.',2.00,0.50,23,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2224,5,'Which collection stores only unique values?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','A Set stores unique values and automatically ignores duplicate entries.',2.00,0.50,24,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2225,5,'Which collection stores key-value pairs and allows keys of any type?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','Map stores key-value pairs and supports keys of any JavaScript value type.',2.00,0.50,25,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2226,5,'Which method adds a value to a Set?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','The add() method adds a value to a Set.',2.00,0.50,26,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2227,5,'Which method adds a key-value pair to a Map?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','The Map set() method adds or updates a key-value pair.',2.00,0.50,27,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2228,5,'What does a Promise represent?','Promises','SINGLE_CHOICE','A Promise represents the eventual completion or failure of an asynchronous operation.',2.00,0.50,28,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2229,5,'Which method is used to handle a fulfilled Promise?','Promises','SINGLE_CHOICE','The then() method registers a callback to handle a fulfilled Promise.',2.00,0.50,29,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2230,5,'Which method is used to handle a rejected Promise?','Promises','SINGLE_CHOICE','The catch() method handles rejected Promises.',2.00,0.50,30,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2231,5,'Which keyword is used to declare an asynchronous function?','Async/Await','SINGLE_CHOICE','The async keyword declares a function that returns a Promise.',2.00,0.50,31,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2232,5,'Which keyword waits for a Promise to settle inside an async function?','Async/Await','SINGLE_CHOICE','The await keyword pauses execution within an async function until the Promise settles.',2.00,0.50,32,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2233,5,'Which array method creates a new array by transforming every element?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The map() method applies a callback to each element and returns a new array.',2.00,0.50,33,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2234,5,'Which array method returns elements that satisfy a condition?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The filter() method creates a new array containing elements that pass the callback condition.',2.00,0.50,34,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2235,5,'Which array method reduces an array to a single accumulated value?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The reduce() method applies a reducer function to produce a single accumulated result.',2.00,0.50,35,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2236,5,'Which array method returns the first element that satisfies a condition?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The find() method returns the first array element for which the callback returns true.',2.00,0.50,36,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2237,5,'Which array method checks whether at least one element satisfies a condition?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The some() method returns true if at least one element passes the supplied test.',2.00,0.50,37,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2238,5,'Which array method checks whether all elements satisfy a condition?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The every() method returns true only when all elements pass the supplied test.',2.00,0.50,38,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2239,5,'What is a closure in JavaScript?','Functions & Closures','SINGLE_CHOICE','A closure allows a function to retain access to variables from its surrounding lexical scope.',2.00,0.50,39,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2240,5,'What is hoisting in JavaScript?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','Hoisting describes JavaScript\'s processing of certain declarations before execution of the code.',2.00,0.50,40,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2241,5,'What is the Temporal Dead Zone associated with?','Scope & Hoisting','SINGLE_CHOICE','let and const declarations are in a Temporal Dead Zone from the start of their block until initialization.',2.00,0.50,41,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2242,5,'What does the this keyword generally refer to?','this Keyword','SINGLE_CHOICE','The value of this depends on how a function is called and the execution context.',2.00,0.50,42,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2243,5,'How does this behave differently inside an arrow function?','Arrow Functions','SINGLE_CHOICE','Arrow functions do not have their own this binding; they inherit this from their surrounding lexical scope.',2.00,0.50,43,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2244,5,'Which operator provides a fallback only when the left value is null or undefined?','Modern JavaScript','SINGLE_CHOICE','The nullish coalescing operator ?? uses the right-hand value only when the left-hand value is null or undefined.',2.00,0.50,44,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2245,5,'Which operator safely accesses a property when an object may be null or undefined?','Modern JavaScript','SINGLE_CHOICE','Optional chaining (?.) prevents an error when accessing properties through null or undefined values.',2.00,0.50,45,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2246,5,'Which statement is used to throw a custom error in JavaScript?','Error Handling','SINGLE_CHOICE','The throw statement is used to throw an exception or custom error.',2.00,0.50,46,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2247,5,'Which block is used to handle an exception thrown by JavaScript code?','Error Handling','SINGLE_CHOICE','The catch block handles exceptions generated inside the corresponding try block.',2.00,0.50,47,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2248,5,'Which block executes whether an exception occurs or not?','Error Handling','SINGLE_CHOICE','The finally block executes after try and catch processing regardless of whether an exception occurred.',2.00,0.50,48,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2249,5,'Which ES6 feature allows a function to have default values for parameters?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Default parameters allow a function parameter to have a predefined value when no argument is provided.',2.00,0.50,49,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2250,5,'What is the output of: const x = [1, 2]; const y = [...x, 3];','Spread Operator','SINGLE_CHOICE','The spread syntax expands the elements of x, producing [1, 2, 3].',2.00,0.50,50,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2251,5,'What is the output of: const [a, b] = [10, 20];','Destructuring','SINGLE_CHOICE','Array destructuring assigns the first element to a and the second element to b.',2.00,0.50,51,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2252,5,'What is the output of: const { name } = { name: \'Ajay\', age: 23 };','Destructuring','SINGLE_CHOICE','Object destructuring extracts the value of the name property and assigns \'Ajay\' to name.',2.00,0.50,52,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2253,5,'Which keyword is used to define a generator function?','Generators','SINGLE_CHOICE','A generator function is declared using function* and can pause execution using yield.',2.00,0.50,53,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2254,5,'Which keyword pauses a generator function and provides a value to its iterator?','Generators','SINGLE_CHOICE','The yield keyword pauses generator execution and produces a value for the iterator.',2.00,0.50,54,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2255,5,'Which ES6 feature provides a unique primitive value that can be used as an object property key?','ES6 Data Types','SINGLE_CHOICE','Symbol creates unique primitive values that can be used as property keys.',2.00,0.50,55,'2026-10-03 02:42:09'),(2256,11,'Which keyword is used to declare a block-scoped variable whose value can be reassigned?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','The let keyword declares a block-scoped variable that can be reassigned.',2.00,0.50,1,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2257,11,'Which keyword is used to declare a block-scoped variable that cannot be reassigned?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','The const keyword creates a block-scoped binding that cannot be reassigned.',2.00,0.50,2,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2258,11,'Which keyword was traditionally used for function-scoped variable declarations?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','The var keyword declares variables with function scope rather than block scope.',2.00,0.50,3,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2259,11,'What does typeof null return in JavaScript?','Data Types','SINGLE_CHOICE','Due to a historical behavior in JavaScript, typeof null returns \"object\".',2.00,0.50,4,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2260,11,'Which operator performs strict equality comparison in JavaScript?','Operators','SINGLE_CHOICE','The === operator compares both value and type without performing type coercion.',2.00,0.50,5,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2261,11,'What is the result of 5 === \'5\'?','Operators','SINGLE_CHOICE','The values have different types, so strict equality returns false.',2.00,0.50,6,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2262,11,'What is the result of 5 == \'5\'?','Type Coercion','SINGLE_CHOICE','The == operator performs type coercion before comparison, making 5 and \'5\' equal.',2.00,0.50,7,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2263,11,'Which value represents the absence of an assigned value?','Data Types','SINGLE_CHOICE','undefined commonly indicates that a variable has been declared but has not been assigned a value.',2.00,0.50,8,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2264,11,'Which value represents an intentional absence of an object value?','Data Types','SINGLE_CHOICE','null is commonly used to explicitly indicate that a value is intentionally absent.',2.00,0.50,9,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2265,11,'Which ES6 feature provides a shorter syntax for writing functions?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Arrow functions provide a concise syntax for defining functions.',2.00,0.50,10,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2266,11,'Which syntax is used to create a template literal?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Template literals are enclosed in backticks and support embedded expressions.',2.00,0.50,11,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2267,11,'Which syntax is used to insert an expression inside a template literal?','Template Literals','SINGLE_CHOICE','Expressions are embedded in template literals using ${expression}.',2.00,0.50,12,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2268,11,'What is destructuring in JavaScript?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Destructuring allows values from arrays or properties from objects to be assigned directly to variables.',2.00,0.50,13,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2269,11,'Which operator is used for the spread syntax?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','The three-dot syntax (...) is used for spread and rest operations.',2.00,0.50,14,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2270,11,'What does the spread syntax do when used with an array?','Spread Operator','SINGLE_CHOICE','Spread syntax expands the elements of an iterable into individual elements.',2.00,0.50,15,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2271,11,'Which syntax collects multiple function arguments into an array?','Rest Parameters','SINGLE_CHOICE','A rest parameter such as ...args collects remaining function arguments into an array.',2.00,0.50,16,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2272,11,'Which keyword is used to define a class in ES6?','Classes','SINGLE_CHOICE','ES6 introduced the class syntax for defining classes.',2.00,0.50,17,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2273,11,'Which method is automatically called when a new class instance is created?','Classes','SINGLE_CHOICE','The constructor() method is called automatically when an object is created using new.',2.00,0.50,18,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2274,11,'Which keyword is used to inherit from another class?','Classes & Inheritance','SINGLE_CHOICE','The extends keyword is used to create a subclass of another class.',2.00,0.50,19,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2275,11,'Which keyword is used to access the parent class constructor or methods?','Classes & Inheritance','SINGLE_CHOICE','The super keyword is used to call the parent constructor or access parent methods.',2.00,0.50,20,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2276,11,'Which keyword is used to export functionality from an ES6 module?','Modules','SINGLE_CHOICE','The export keyword makes declarations available to other modules.',2.00,0.50,21,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2277,11,'Which keyword is used to import functionality from another ES6 module?','Modules','SINGLE_CHOICE','The import keyword is used to import exported bindings from another module.',2.00,0.50,22,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2278,11,'Which statement correctly imports a default export named calculate?','Modules','SINGLE_CHOICE','A default export is imported without curly braces.',2.00,0.50,23,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2279,11,'Which collection stores only unique values?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','A Set stores unique values and automatically ignores duplicate entries.',2.00,0.50,24,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2280,11,'Which collection stores key-value pairs and allows keys of any type?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','Map stores key-value pairs and supports keys of any JavaScript value type.',2.00,0.50,25,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2281,11,'Which method adds a value to a Set?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','The add() method adds a value to a Set.',2.00,0.50,26,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2282,11,'Which method adds a key-value pair to a Map?','ES6 Collections','SINGLE_CHOICE','The Map set() method adds or updates a key-value pair.',2.00,0.50,27,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2283,11,'What does a Promise represent?','Promises','SINGLE_CHOICE','A Promise represents the eventual completion or failure of an asynchronous operation.',2.00,0.50,28,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2284,11,'Which method is used to handle a fulfilled Promise?','Promises','SINGLE_CHOICE','The then() method registers a callback to handle a fulfilled Promise.',2.00,0.50,29,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2285,11,'Which method is used to handle a rejected Promise?','Promises','SINGLE_CHOICE','The catch() method handles rejected Promises.',2.00,0.50,30,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2286,11,'Which keyword is used to declare an asynchronous function?','Async/Await','SINGLE_CHOICE','The async keyword declares a function that returns a Promise.',2.00,0.50,31,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2287,11,'Which keyword waits for a Promise to settle inside an async function?','Async/Await','SINGLE_CHOICE','The await keyword pauses execution within an async function until the Promise settles.',2.00,0.50,32,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2288,11,'Which array method creates a new array by transforming every element?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The map() method applies a callback to each element and returns a new array.',2.00,0.50,33,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2289,11,'Which array method returns elements that satisfy a condition?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The filter() method creates a new array containing elements that pass the callback condition.',2.00,0.50,34,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2290,11,'Which array method reduces an array to a single accumulated value?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The reduce() method applies a reducer function to produce a single accumulated result.',2.00,0.50,35,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2291,11,'Which array method returns the first element that satisfies a condition?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The find() method returns the first array element for which the callback returns true.',2.00,0.50,36,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2292,11,'Which array method checks whether at least one element satisfies a condition?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The some() method returns true if at least one element passes the supplied test.',2.00,0.50,37,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2293,11,'Which array method checks whether all elements satisfy a condition?','Array Methods','SINGLE_CHOICE','The every() method returns true only when all elements pass the supplied test.',2.00,0.50,38,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2294,11,'What is a closure in JavaScript?','Functions & Closures','SINGLE_CHOICE','A closure allows a function to retain access to variables from its surrounding lexical scope.',2.00,0.50,39,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2295,11,'What is hoisting in JavaScript?','JavaScript Core','SINGLE_CHOICE','Hoisting describes JavaScript\'s processing of certain declarations before execution of the code.',2.00,0.50,40,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2296,11,'What is the Temporal Dead Zone associated with?','Scope & Hoisting','SINGLE_CHOICE','let and const declarations are in a Temporal Dead Zone from the start of their block until initialization.',2.00,0.50,41,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2297,11,'What does the this keyword generally refer to?','this Keyword','SINGLE_CHOICE','The value of this depends on how a function is called and the execution context.',2.00,0.50,42,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2298,11,'How does this behave differently inside an arrow function?','Arrow Functions','SINGLE_CHOICE','Arrow functions do not have their own this binding; they inherit this from their surrounding lexical scope.',2.00,0.50,43,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2299,11,'Which operator provides a fallback only when the left value is null or undefined?','Modern JavaScript','SINGLE_CHOICE','The nullish coalescing operator ?? uses the right-hand value only when the left-hand value is null or undefined.',2.00,0.50,44,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2300,11,'Which operator safely accesses a property when an object may be null or undefined?','Modern JavaScript','SINGLE_CHOICE','Optional chaining (?.) prevents an error when accessing properties through null or undefined values.',2.00,0.50,45,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2301,11,'Which statement is used to throw a custom error in JavaScript?','Error Handling','SINGLE_CHOICE','The throw statement is used to throw an exception or custom error.',2.00,0.50,46,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2302,11,'Which block is used to handle an exception thrown by JavaScript code?','Error Handling','SINGLE_CHOICE','The catch block handles exceptions generated inside the corresponding try block.',2.00,0.50,47,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2303,11,'Which block executes whether an exception occurs or not?','Error Handling','SINGLE_CHOICE','The finally block executes after try and catch processing regardless of whether an exception occurred.',2.00,0.50,48,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2304,11,'Which ES6 feature allows a function to have default values for parameters?','ES6 Features','SINGLE_CHOICE','Default parameters allow a function parameter to have a predefined value when no argument is provided.',2.00,0.50,49,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2305,11,'What is the output of: const x = [1, 2]; const y = [...x, 3];','Spread Operator','SINGLE_CHOICE','The spread syntax expands the elements of x, producing [1, 2, 3].',2.00,0.50,50,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2306,11,'What is the output of: const [a, b] = [10, 20];','Destructuring','SINGLE_CHOICE','Array destructuring assigns the first element to a and the second element to b.',2.00,0.50,51,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2307,11,'What is the output of: const { name } = { name: \'Ajay\', age: 23 };','Destructuring','SINGLE_CHOICE','Object destructuring extracts the value of the name property and assigns \'Ajay\' to name.',2.00,0.50,52,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2308,11,'Which keyword is used to define a generator function?','Generators','SINGLE_CHOICE','A generator function is declared using function* and can pause execution using yield.',2.00,0.50,53,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2309,11,'Which keyword pauses a generator function and provides a value to its iterator?','Generators','SINGLE_CHOICE','The yield keyword pauses generator execution and produces a value for the iterator.',2.00,0.50,54,'2026-10-03 02:44:38'),(2310,11,'Which ES6 feature provides a unique primitive value that can be used as an object property key?','ES6 Data Types','SINGLE_CHOICE','Symbol creates unique primitive values that can be used as property keys.',2.00,0.50,55,'2026-10-03 02:44:38');
