 data-question=\"39\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>39. What is malware?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,39,0)\"><b>A.</b> Malicious software</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,39,1)\"><b>B.</b> Memory hardware</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,39,2)\"><b>C.</b> A network cable</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,39,3)\"><b>D.</b> A database key</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback39\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"40\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>40. What is phishing?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,40,0)\"><b>A.</b> A deceptive attempt to obtain information by pretending to be trustworthy</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,40,1)\"><b>B.</b> A disk scheduling method</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,40,2)\"><b>C.</b> A CPU operation</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,40,3)\"><b>D.</b> A type of RAM</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback40\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"41\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>41. What does MFA provide?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,41,0)\"><b>A.</b> An additional authentication factor beyond a single credential</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,41,1)\"><b>B.</b> More RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,41,2)\"><b>C.</b> Faster CPU execution</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,41,3)\"><b>D.</b> Automatic backups only</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback41\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"42\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>42. What does confidentiality mean in the CIA triad?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,42,0)\"><b>A.</b> Authorized parties can access information</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,42,1)\"><b>B.</b> Data is always available</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,42,2)\"><b>C.</b> Data is compressed</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,42,3)\"><b>D.</b> CPU is fast</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback42\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"43\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>43. What does integrity mean in cybersecurity?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,43,0)\"><b>A.</b> Information remains accurate and unaltered improperly</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,43,1)\"><b>B.</b> Every system is online</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,43,2)\"><b>C.</b> Files are always compressed</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,43,3)\"><b>D.</b> Passwords are public</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback43\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"44\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>44. What does availability mean?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,44,0)\"><b>A.</b> Systems and information are accessible when needed</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,44,1)\"><b>B.</b> Only administrators can use a system</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,44,2)\"><b>C.</b> Data is always encrypted</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,44,3)\"><b>D.</b> A CPU never stops</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback44\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"45\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>45. What is a database?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,45,0)\"><b>A.</b> An organized collection of data</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,45,1)\"><b>B.</b> A computer monitor</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,45,2)\"><b>C.</b> A CPU register</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,45,3)\"><b>D.</b> A network cable</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback45\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"46\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>46. What does DBMS stand for?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,46,0)\"><b>A.</b> Database Management System</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,46,1)\"><b>B.</b> Data Backup Memory Service</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,46,2)\"><b>C.</b> Digital Binary Management Software</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,46,3)\"><b>D.</b> Database Machine Storage</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback46\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"47\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>47. What is a primary key?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,47,0)\"><b>A.</b> A column or set of columns that uniquely identifies a row</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,47,1)\"><b>B.</b> A password for the computer</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,47,2)\"><b>C.</b> A network cable</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,47,3)\"><b>D.</b> A file extension</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback47\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"48\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>48. What is a foreign key?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,48,0)\"><b>A.</b> A field that references a key in another table</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,48,1)\"><b>B.</b> A CPU register</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,48,2)\"><b>C.</b> A type of monitor</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,48,3)\"><b>D.</b> A network address</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback48\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"49\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>49. Which SQL command retrieves data?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,49,0)\"><b>A.</b> SELECT</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,49,1)\"><b>B.</b> DELETE</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,49,2)\"><b>C.</b> CREATE</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,49,3)\"><b>D.</b> DROP</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback49\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"50\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>50. Which is a good basic security practice?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,50,0)\"><b>A.</b> Use strong unique passwords and MFA</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,50,1)\"><b>B.</b> Share passwords publicly</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,50,2)\"><b>C.</b> Disable all updates</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,50,3)\"><b>D.</b> Open unknown attachments</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback50\"></div></article>\n</main>\n\n<footer>Computer Fundamentals · Lightweight Interactive HTML Notes · Works Offline</footer>\n\n<script>\nconst questions=[\n[\"What is the basic computer cycle?\",[\"Input → Process → Output\",\"Output → Input → Process\",\"Process → Output → Input\",\"Storage → Output → Input\"],0],\n[\"Which component executes instructions?\",[\"Monitor\",\"CPU\",\"Keyboard\",\"Printer\"],1],\n[\"Which memory is normally volatile?\",[\"RAM\",\"SSD\",\"ROM\",\"Optical disc\"],0],\n[\"What does an operating system manage?\",[\"Only documents\",\"Only websites\",\"Hardware and system resources\",\"Only keyboards\"],2],\n[\"Which device forwards traffic between networks?\",[\"Router\",\"Keyboard\",\"Monitor\",\"Scanner\"],0],\n[\"What does DNS primarily do?\",[\"Compress files\",\"Translate domain names to IP addresses\",\"Create passwords\",\"Print documents\"],1],\n[\"Which is part of the CIA security triad?\",[\"Caching\",\"Confidentiality\",\"Compilation\",\"Calculation\"],1],\n[\"Which key uniquely identifies a relational table row?\",[\"Primary key\",\"CSS key\",\"Network key\",\"Display key\"],0]\n];\ndocument.getElementById(\"quiz\").innerHTML=questions.map((q,i)=>`\n<div class=\"card quiz\"><h3>${i+1}. ${q[0]}</h3>\n${q[1].map((x,j)=>`<button onclick=\"check(this,${i},${j})\">${x}</button>`).join(\"\")}\n<div class=\"result\" id=\"r${i}\"></div></div>`).join(\"\");\nfunction check(btn,i,j){\n const box=btn.parentElement;if(box.dataset.done)return;box.dataset.done=\"1\";\n if(j===questions[i][2]){btn.style.background=\"#dcfce7\";btn.style.borderColor=\"#86efac\";document.getElementById(\"r\"+i).textContent=\"Correct ✓\";}\n else{btn.style.background=\"#fee2e2\";btn.style.borderColor=\"#fca5a5\";document.getElementById(\"r\"+i).textContent=\"Correct answer: \"+questions[i][1][questions[i][2]];}\n}\nconst observer=new IntersectionObserver(es=>es.forEach(e=>{if(e.isIntersecting)e.target.classList.add(\"show\")}),{threshold:.08});\ndocument.querySelectorAll(\".reveal\").forEach(x=>observer.observe(x));\n\nlet quizCorrect=0,quizAnswered=0;\nfunction answerQuestion(btn,num,index){\n  const card=btn.closest(\'.quiz-card\');\n  if(card.dataset.done)return;\n  card.dataset.done=\"1\";quizAnswered++;\n  const answer=Number(card.dataset.answer);\n  const buttons=[...card.querySelectorAll(\'.quiz-option\')];\n  buttons[answer].classList.add(\'correct\');\n  const feedback=document.getElementById(\'feedback\'+num);\n  if(index===answer){\n    quizCorrect++;\n    feedback.textContent=\'✓ Correct! \'+questions50[num-1][3];\n  }else{\n    btn.classList.add(\'wrong\');\n    feedback.textContent=\'Correct answer: \'+String.fromCharCode(65+answer)+\'. \'+questions50[num-1][1][answer]+\' — \'+questions50[num-1][3];\n  }\n  document.getElementById(\'quizScore\').textContent=\'Score: \'+quizCorrect+\' / 50 · Answered: \'+quizAnswered+\' / 50\';\n}\nfunction resetQuiz(){\n  quizCorrect=0;quizAnswered=0;\n  document.getElementById(\'quizScore\').textContent=\'Score: 0 / 50\';\n  document.querySelectorAll(\'.quiz-card\').forEach(card=>{\n    delete card.dataset.done;\n    card.querySelectorAll(\'.quiz-option\').forEach(b=>b.classList.remove(\'correct\',\'wrong\'));\n    card.querySelector(\'.quiz-feedback\').textContent=\'\';\n  });\n}\nconst questions50=[[\"Which sequence represents the basic working cycle of a computer?\", [\"Input → Process → Output\", \"Output → Process → Input\", \"Process → Input → Output\", \"Input → Output → Process\"], 0, \"A computer generally accepts input, processes it, and produces output.\"], [\"Which unit is primarily responsible for executing program instructions?\", [\"RAM\", \"CPU\", \"Monitor\", \"Keyboard\"], 1, \"The CPU executes instructions and performs calculations and control operations.\"], [\"What does CPU stand for?\", [\"Central Processing Unit\", \"Computer Processing Utility\", \"Central Program Unit\", \"Core Processing User\"], 0, \"CPU means Central Processing Unit.\"], [\"Which component performs arithmetic and logical operations?\", [\"Control Unit\", \"ALU\", \"RAM\", \"Power Supply\"], 1, \"The Arithmetic Logic Unit performs arithmetic and logical operations.\"], [\"What is the main function of the Control Unit?\", [\"Store files permanently\", \"Perform arithmetic only\", \"Coordinate instruction execution\", \"Display images\"], 2, \"The Control Unit coordinates and directs CPU operations.\"], [\"Which is the fastest storage location among these?\", [\"Hard disk\", \"RAM\", \"CPU register\", \"USB drive\"], 2, \"CPU registers are extremely small and very fast storage locations inside the processor.\"], [\"Which memory is normally volatile?\", [\"ROM\", \"RAM\", \"SSD\", \"DVD\"], 1, \"RAM loses its stored contents when power is removed.\"], [\"What is the main purpose of RAM?\", [\"Permanent file storage\", \"Temporary working storage for active programs\", \"Printing documents\", \"Connecting networks\"], 1, \"RAM holds programs and data currently being used by the system.\"], [\"Which storage device normally retains data after power is removed?\", [\"RAM\", \"Cache\", \"Register\", \"SSD\"], 3, \"SSD is non-volatile secondary storage.\"], [\"What is cache memory used for?\", [\"Long-term backup\", \"Speeding access to frequently used data/instructions\", \"Printing\", \"Network routing\"], 1, \"Cache stores frequently or recently used information close to the CPU for faster access.\"], [\"Which device is an input device?\", [\"Monitor\", \"Printer\", \"Keyboard\", \"Speaker\"], 2, \"A keyboard sends data and commands into the computer.\"], [\"Which device is an output device?\", [\"Mouse\", \"Scanner\", \"Microphone\", \"Monitor\"], 3, \"A monitor displays processed information to the user.\"], [\"What is a motherboard?\", [\"A software program\", \"The main circuit board connecting computer components\", \"A storage file\", \"A network protocol\"], 1, \"The motherboard connects major components and provides communication pathways.\"], [\"Which component is commonly used for long-term data storage?\", [\"RAM\", \"CPU register\", \"SSD\", \"Cache\"], 2, \"An SSD provides persistent storage.\"], [\"What is hardware?\", [\"Physical computer components\", \"Only operating systems\", \"Only applications\", \"Internet data\"], 0, \"Hardware refers to physical components that can be physically handled.\"], [\"What is software?\", [\"Physical circuitry\", \"Programs and instructions\", \"Only cables\", \"A power source\"], 1, \"Software consists of programs and instructions executed by a computer.\"], [\"Which is an example of system software?\", [\"Operating system\", \"Photo\", \"Music file\", \"Spreadsheet document\"], 0, \"An operating system is system software that manages hardware and provides services.\"], [\"Which is an example of application software?\", [\"Device driver\", \"Operating system\", \"Web browser\", \"Boot firmware\"], 2, \"A web browser is application software used for a user task.\"], [\"What does a compiler generally do?\", [\"Translates source code before execution\", \"Prints source code\", \"Stores files\", \"Connects Wi-Fi\"], 0, \"A compiler translates source code into another form before execution.\"], [\"What does an interpreter generally do?\", [\"Physically repairs hardware\", \"Executes/translates program instructions at runtime\", \"Provides electrical power\", \"Formats a monitor\"], 1, \"An interpreter processes program instructions during execution.\"], [\"What is the main role of an operating system?\", [\"Manage resources and provide services to programs\", \"Only browse the Internet\", \"Only edit images\", \"Only store music\"], 0, \"The OS manages CPU, memory, files, devices, security and other resources.\"], [\"Which is an operating system function?\", [\"Process management\", \"Screen cleaning\", \"Keyboard manufacturing\", \"Cable production\"], 0, \"Process management is a core OS responsibility.\"], [\"What is a process?\", [\"A program in execution\", \"A keyboard key\", \"A storage cable\", \"A network port\"], 0, \"A process is a running instance of a program.\"], [\"What does GUI stand for?\", [\"Graphical User Interface\", \"General Utility Input\", \"Global User Internet\", \"Graphic Unit Instruction\"], 0, \"GUI means Graphical User Interface.\"], [\"What does CLI stand for?\", [\"Command Line Interface\", \"Computer Logic Input\", \"Central Link Internet\", \"Control Language Instruction\"], 0, \"CLI means Command Line Interface.\"], [\"What does I/O mean?\", [\"Input/Output\", \"Internet/Online\", \"Internal/Operating\", \"Instruction/Order\"], 0, \"I/O stands for Input/Output.\"], [\"Which is an input device used to capture sound?\", [\"Speaker\", \"Microphone\", \"Monitor\", \"Projector\"], 1, \"A microphone captures audio as input.\"], [\"Which device produces printed output?\", [\"Scanner\", \"Printer\", \"Keyboard\", \"Mouse\"], 1, \"A printer produces physical printed output.\"], [\"What is a computer network?\", [\"A group of connected devices that communicate\", \"A single CPU\", \"A type of RAM\", \"A text editor\"], 0, \"A network connects devices so they can exchange data and share resources.\"], [\"What does LAN stand for?\", [\"Local Area Network\", \"Large Access Node\", \"Logical Area Number\", \"Local Application Network\"], 0, \"LAN means Local Area Network.\"], [\"What does WAN stand for?\", [\"Wide Area Network\", \"Wireless Application Node\", \"Web Access Network\", \"Wide Application Number\"], 0, \"WAN means Wide Area Network.\"], [\"Which device forwards packets between different networks?\", [\"Switch\", \"Router\", \"Keyboard\", \"Printer\"], 1, \"A router forwards traffic between networks.\"], [\"What is the main role of a network switch?\", [\"Connect devices within a network\", \"Execute CPU instructions\", \"Store operating systems\", \"Print documents\"], 0, \"A switch connects devices and forwards traffic within a local network.\"], [\"What does an IP address identify?\", [\"A network interface/device address\", \"A file extension\", \"A CPU instruction\", \"A keyboard layout\"], 0, \"An IP address identifies a network interface for communication.\"], [\"What does DNS primarily do?\", [\"Translate domain names to IP addresses\", \"Encrypt every file\", \"Create RAM\", \"Print web pages\"], 0, \"DNS resolves human-readable domain names to IP addresses.\"], [\"What does URL stand for?\", [\"Uniform Resource Locator\", \"Universal Router Link\", \"User Resource Language\", \"Unified Runtime Location\"], 0, \"URL means Uniform Resource Locator.\"], [\"What is HTTPS?\", [\"A secure version of HTTP using encryption mechanisms\", \"A type of RAM\", \"A CPU instruction\", \"A database table\"], 0, \"HTTPS protects web communication using TLS encryption.\"], [\"Which protocol is commonly used to transfer web pages?\", [\"HTTP\", \"RAM\", \"CPU\", \"BIOS\"], 0, \"HTTP is a protocol used for web communication.\"], [\"What is malware?\", [\"Malicious software\", \"Memory hardware\", \"A network cable\", \"A database key\"], 0, \"Malware is software designed to harm, disrupt, spy on, or gain unauthorized access to systems.\"], [\"What is phishing?\", [\"A deceptive attempt to obtain information by pretending to be trustworthy\", \"A disk scheduling method\", \"A CPU operation\", \"A type of RAM\"], 0, \"Phishing commonly uses deceptive messages or sites to trick people into revealing information.\"], [\"What does MFA provide?\", [\"An additional authentication factor beyond a single credential\", \"More RAM\", \"Faster CPU execution\", \"Automatic backups only\"], 0, \"Multi-factor authentication requires multiple forms of evidence to verify identity.\"], [\"What does confidentiality mean in the CIA triad?\", [\"Authorized parties can access information\", \"Data is always available\", \"Data is compressed\", \"CPU is fast\"], 0, \"Confidentiality focuses on preventing unauthorized access to information.\"], [\"What does integrity mean in cybersecurity?\", [\"Information remains accurate and unaltered improperly\", \"Every system is online\", \"Files are always compressed\", \"Passwords are public\"], 0, \"Integrity protects information from unauthorized or unintended modification.\"], [\"What does availability mean?\", [\"Systems and information are accessible when needed\", \"Only administrators can use a system\", \"Data is always encrypted\", \"A CPU never stops\"], 0, \"Availability focuses on reliable access to systems and information.\"], [\"What is a database?\", [\"An organized collection of data\", \"A computer monitor\", \"A CPU register\", \"A network cable\"], 0, \"A database organizes data so it can be stored, queried and updated.\"], [\"What does DBMS stand for?\", [\"Database Management System\", \"Data Backup Memory Service\", \"Digital Binary Management Software\", \"Database Machine Storage\"], 0, \"DBMS means Database Management System.\"], [\"What is a primary key?\", [\"A column or set of columns that uniquely identifies a row\", \"A password for the computer\", \"A network cable\", \"A file extension\"], 0, \"A primary key uniquely identifies records in a relational table.\"], [\"What is a foreign key?\", [\"A field that references a key in another table\", \"A CPU register\", \"A type of monitor\", \"A network address\"], 0, \"A foreign key represents a relationship by referencing a key in another table.\"], [\"Which SQL command retrieves data?\", [\"SELECT\", \"DELETE\", \"CREATE\", \"DROP\"], 0, \"SELECT is used to query and retrieve data from tables.\"], [\"Which is a good basic security practice?\", [\"Use strong unique passwords and MFA\", \"Share passwords publicly\", \"Disable all updates\", \"Open unknown attachments\"], 0, \"Strong unique passwords, MFA, updates and cautious handling of links/files improve security.\"]];\n\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>',1,0.00,0.00,0.00,NULL,'SELECTED_CENTRES','BOTH',NULL,'PUBLISHED',NULL,1,'center',1,0,0,'2026-10-04 14:37:32','2026-10-04 15:23:20',20.00),(19,'TEST','test-133','Programming','TEST APPROVAL',NULL,'','HTML','2.5 MB','<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#0f172a\">\n<title>Computer Fundamentals — Interactive Notes</title>\n<style>\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth}\nbody{margin:0;font-family:Inter,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif;background:#f5f7fb;color:#172033;line-height:1.6}\nheader{background:#0f172a;color:#fff;padding:38px 20px}\n.wrap{max-width:1080px;margin:auto}\nh1{font-size:clamp(32px,6vw,58px);line-height:1.05;margin:0 0 12px}\nh2{font-size:28px;margin:0;color:#0f172a}h3{margin:0 0 8px}\nheader p{max-width:780px;color:#cbd5e1;margin:0}\nnav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:10;background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid #e2e8f0}\n.nav{max-width:1080px;margin:auto;display:flex;gap:5px;overflow:auto;padding:9px}\nnav a{white-space:nowrap;color:#475569;text-decoration:none;padding:7px 10px;border-radius:7px;font-size:14px}\nnav a:hover{background:#e0f2fe;color:#0369a1}\nmain{max-width:1080px;margin:auto;padding:25px 16px 60px}\nsection{margin:32px 0;scroll-margin-top:65px}\n.sub{color:#64748b;margin:3px 0 15px}\n.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:14px}\n.card{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:14px;padding:19px;box-shadow:0 4px 16px #0f172a08}\n.card:hover{transform:translateY(-2px);transition:.2s;box-shadow:0 8px 22px #0f172a12}\n.flow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:15px 0}\n.box{background:#eff6ff;border:1px solid #bfdbfe;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 14px;font-weight:700;text-align:center}\n.arrow{font-size:21px;color:#0284c7}\n.badge{display:inline-block;background:#e0f2fe;color:#0369a1;border-radius:99px;padding:3px 8px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;margin:2px}\n.green{background:#dcfce7;color:#166534}.yellow{background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e}.pink{background:#fce7f3;color:#9d174d}\n.tip{background:#f0f9ff;border-left:4px solid #0ea5e9;padding:10px 13px;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0}\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}th,td{text-align:left;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid #e2e8f0}th{background:#f8fafc}\ncode,pre{background:#0f172a;color:#dbeafe;border-radius:8px;padding:2px 5px}\npre{padding:14px;overflow:auto}\n.quiz button{display:block;width:100%;text-align:left;border:1px solid #dbe2ea;background:#f8fafc;padding:10px;border-radius:8px;margin:7px 0;cursor:pointer}\n.quiz button:hover{background:#e0f2fe;border-color:#7dd3fc}\n.result{font-weight:700;margin-top:8px}\n.reveal{opacity:0;transform:translateY(12px)}.show{opacity:1;transform:none;transition:.5s ease}\nfooter{text-align:center;color:#64748b;padding:35px}\n@media(max-width:720px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.flow{justify-content:flex-start}}\n@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{scroll-behavior:auto!important;transition:none!important}}\n\n.quiz-tools{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:10px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:12px;padding:12px;margin:12px 0 15px;position:sticky;top:55px;z-index:5}\n.quiz-tools button{border:1px solid #cbd5e1;background:#f8fafc;padding:8px 12px;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer}\n.quiz-option{transition:.18s}\n.quiz-option.correct{background:#dcfce7!important;border-color:#86efac!important;color:#166534}\n.quiz-option.wrong{background:#fee2e2!important;border-color:#fca5a5!important;color:#991b1b}\n.quiz-feedback{min-height:24px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-top:7px;color:#475569}\n.quiz-card{margin-bottom:12px}\n</style>\n\n<style id=\"handwritten-modern-theme\">\n\n\n:root{\n  --paper:#fffdf7;\n  --paper2:#fff9ed;\n  --ink:#263238;\n  --muted:#66727a;\n  --blue:#2563eb;\n  --cyan:#0891b2;\n  --purple:#7c3aed;\n  --pink:#db2777;\n  --green:#15803d;\n  --yellow:#facc15;\n  --orange:#ea580c;\n  --border:#d9d2c3;\n  --shadow:4px 5px 0 rgba(38,50,56,.09);\n}\nbody{\n  background:\n    linear-gradient(rgba(37,99,235,.045) 1px,transparent 1px),\n    linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(37,99,235,.045) 1px,transparent 1px),\n    #f8f5ed;\n  background-size:28px 28px;\n  color:var(--ink);\n  font-family:\'Nunito\',system-ui,sans-serif;\n}\nheader{\n  background:#172554;\n  position:relative;\n  overflow:hidden;\n  border-bottom:5px solid #facc15;\n}\nheader:after{\n  content:\"✦  learn • sketch • understand  ✦\";\n  position:absolute;\n  right:4%;\n  bottom:18px;\n  color:#bfdbfe;\n  font:600 20px \'Caveat\',cursive;\n  transform:rotate(-4deg);\n}\nheader h1{\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',\'Caveat\',cursive;\n  font-weight:700;\n  letter-spacing:.5px;\n}\nheader p{font-family:\'Nunito\',sans-serif}\nnav{\n  background:#fffdf7;\n  border-bottom:2px solid var(--border);\n}\nnav a{\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',cursive;\n  font-size:16px;\n}\nnav a:hover{background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e}\nmain{max-width:1120px}\nsection{position:relative}\nsection h2{\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',\'Caveat\',cursive;\n  font-size:35px;\n  letter-spacing:.2px;\n}\n.sub{font-family:\'Caveat\',cursive;font-size:21px;color:#65727b}\n.card{\n  background:var(--paper);\n  border:2px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius:5px 9px 6px 8px;\n  box-shadow:var(--shadow);\n  position:relative;\n  transform:rotate(-.15deg);\n}\n.card:nth-child(2n){transform:rotate(.18deg)}\n.card:before{\n  content:\"\";\n  position:absolute;\n  width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%;\n  background:#f87171;\n  top:10px;right:12px;\n  opacity:.7;\n}\n.card h3{\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',cursive;\n  font-size:23px;\n}\n.card p,.card li,.card td,.card th{\n  font-family:\'Nunito\',sans-serif;\n}\n.box{\n  background:#eff6ff;\n  border:2px solid #93c5fd;\n  border-radius:5px 8px 5px 7px;\n  box-shadow:2px 2px 0 #bfdbfe;\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',cursive;\n  font-size:17px;\n}\n.arrow{\n  font-family:\'Caveat\',cursive;\n  font-weight:700;\n}\n.badge{\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',cursive;\n  font-size:14px;\n  border:1px dashed currentColor;\n}\n.tip{\n  background:#fff7b8;\n  border-left:0;\n  border-bottom:2px solid #eab308;\n  border-radius:2px;\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',cursive;\n  font-size:17px;\n  transform:rotate(-.5deg);\n  box-shadow:2px 3px 0 rgba(234,179,8,.14);\n}\n.tip:before{content:\"💡 \"}\ntable{background:#fffdf7}\nth{font-family:\'Kalam\',cursive;font-size:17px;background:#fef3c7}\n.diagram,.quiz-tools{\n  background:#fffaf0;\n  border:2px dashed #cfc4ad;\n}\n.quiz-tools{\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',cursive;\n  font-size:18px;\n}\n.quiz-tools button{\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',cursive;\n  font-size:17px;\n  background:#fef3c7;\n  border:2px solid #d6b656;\n}\n.quiz-card{\n  border-left:5px solid #60a5fa;\n}\n.quiz-card h3{\n  font-size:21px;\n}\n.quiz-option{\n  font-family:\'Nunito\',sans-serif;\n  background:#fff;\n  border:1px solid #d8d2c6!important;\n  position:relative;\n}\n.quiz-option:hover{\n  background:#eff6ff!important;\n  border-color:#60a5fa!important;\n  transform:translateX(4px) rotate(-.2deg);\n}\n.quiz-option.correct{\n  background:#dcfce7!important;\n  border-color:#4ade80!important;\n}\n.quiz-option.wrong{\n  background:#fee2e2!important;\n  border-color:#fb7185!important;\n}\n.quiz-feedback{\n  font-family:\'Kalam\',cursive;\n  font-size:18px;\n}\npre{\n  border:2px solid #334155;\n  box-shadow:3px 3px 0 #cbd5e1;\n}\nsection:after{\n  content:\"\";\n  position:absolute;\n  width:80px;\n  height:12px;\n  background:rgba(250,204,21,.35);\n  right:18px;\n  top:8px;\n  transform:rotate(-3deg);\n  pointer-events:none;\n}\nsection:nth-of-type(2n):after{\n  background:rgba(96,165,250,.24);\n  transform:rotate(2deg);\n}\n.hand-note{\n  font:600 22px \'Caveat\',cursive;\n  color:#334155;\n  display:inline-block;\n  transform:rotate(-2deg);\n}\n@keyframes handFloat{\n  50%{transform:translateY(-4px) rotate(-1deg)}\n}\n.card:hover{\n  transform:translateY(-4px) rotate(-.35deg);\n  transition:.28s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1);\n  box-shadow:6px 8px 0 rgba(38,50,56,.1);\n}\n.box:hover{animation:handFloat .7s ease-in-out infinite}\n@media(max-width:700px){\n  header:after{display:none}\n  section h2{font-size:30px}\n}\n@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){\n  .box:hover{animation:none}\n}\n</style>\n\n\n<style id=\"quiz-option-visibility-fix\">\n/* Ensure dynamically added 50-question options remain fully visible. */\n.quiz-card .quiz-option{\n  display:block !important;\n  width:100% !important;\n  min-height:46px;\n  height:auto !important;\n  box-sizing:border-box;\n  text-align:left !important;\n  padding:11px 14px !important;\n  margin:8px 0 !important;\n  background:#fffdf7 !important;\n  color:#263238 !important;\n  border:2px solid #d8d2c6 !important;\n  border-radius:10px !important;\n  font-family:\'Nunito\',system-ui,sans-serif !important;\n  font-size:16px !important;\n  line-height:1.45 !important;\n  white-space:normal !important;\n  overflow:visible !important;\n  opacity:1 !important;\n  visibility:visible !important;\n  cursor:pointer;\n  appearance:none;\n  -webkit-appearance:none;\n}\n.quiz-card .quiz-option b{\n  color:#1d4ed8 !important;\n  font-weight:800;\n  margin-right:5px;\n}\n.quiz-card .quiz-option:hover{\n  background:#eff6ff !important;\n  border-color:#60a5fa !important;\n}\n.quiz-card .quiz-option.correct{\n  background:#dcfce7 !important;\n  color:#166534 !important;\n  border-color:#4ade80 !important;\n}\n.quiz-card .quiz-option.wrong{\n  background:#fee2e2 !important;\n  color:#991b1b !important;\n  border-color:#fb7185 !important;\n}\n@media(max-width:720px){\n  .quiz-card .quiz-option{font-size:15px !important;padding:10px 12px !important;}\n}\n</style>\n\n</head>\n<body>\n<header><div class=\"wrap\">\n<span class=\"badge\" style=\"background:#1e293b;color:#7dd3fc\">BEGINNER FRIENDLY</span><div class=\"hand-note\">✎ simple notes for quick learning</div>\n<h1>Computer Fundamentals</h1>\n<p>Lightweight, visual and exam-friendly notes covering computer basics, hardware, CPU, memory, software, operating systems, networking, Internet, security and databases.</p>\n</div></header>\n\n<nav><div class=\"nav\">\n<a href=\"#basics\">Basics</a><a href=\"#hardware\">Hardware</a><a href=\"#cpu\">CPU</a><a href=\"#memory\">Memory</a>\n<a href=\"#software\">Software</a><a href=\"#os\">OS</a><a href=\"#io\">I/O</a><a href=\"#network\">Networking</a>\n<a href=\"#internet\">Internet</a><a href=\"#security\">Security</a><a href=\"#database\">Database</a><a href=\"#quiz\">Quiz</a>\n</div></nav>\n\n<main>\n<section id=\"basics\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>1. Computer Basics</h2><p class=\"sub\">The basic idea behind every computer system.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>What is a Computer?</h3><p>A computer is an electronic device that accepts data, processes it according to instructions, stores it and produces output.</p>\n<div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">Input</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Process</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Output</div></div>\n<div class=\"tip\"><b>Remember:</b> Input → Processing → Output is the basic working cycle.</div></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Data vs Information</h3><p><b>Data</b> = raw facts.</p><p><b>Information</b> = processed and meaningful data.</p>\n<div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">Raw Data</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Processing</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Information</div></div></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section id=\"hardware\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>2. Computer Hardware</h2><p class=\"sub\">Physical components of a computer.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Main Components</h3><ul><li>Motherboard</li><li>CPU</li><li>RAM</li><li>SSD/HDD</li><li>Power supply</li><li>GPU</li><li>Input and output devices</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Motherboard</h3><p>The motherboard connects major components and provides communication pathways between them.</p>\n<div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">CPU</div><div class=\"box\">RAM</div><div class=\"box\">Storage</div><div class=\"box\">GPU</div></div><div class=\"box\" style=\"width:100%\">MOTHERBOARD</div></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section id=\"cpu\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>3. CPU — Central Processing Unit</h2><p class=\"sub\">The CPU executes program instructions.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>CPU Components</h3><ul><li><b>ALU:</b> arithmetic and logical operations.</li><li><b>Control Unit:</b> coordinates instruction execution.</li><li><b>Registers:</b> very fast CPU storage.</li><li><b>Cache:</b> fast storage close to the CPU.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Instruction Cycle</h3><div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">Fetch</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Decode</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Execute</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Store</div></div><p>The CPU repeatedly performs this cycle while executing instructions.</p></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section id=\"memory\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>4. Computer Memory</h2><p class=\"sub\">Different storage layers have different speed, size and persistence characteristics.</p>\n<div class=\"card\"><table>\n<tr><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Volatile?</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Register</td><td>Very fast CPU storage</td><td>Yes</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cache</td><td>Fast storage near CPU</td><td>Yes</td></tr>\n<tr><td>RAM</td><td>Active programs and data</td><td>Yes</td></tr>\n<tr><td>ROM</td><td>Persistent firmware/instructions</td><td>No</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SSD/HDD</td><td>Long-term storage</td><td>No</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"grid\" style=\"margin-top:14px\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Primary Memory</h3><p>Memory used directly during program execution, especially RAM and cache.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Secondary Storage</h3><p>Persistent storage such as SSDs, HDDs, USB drives and memory cards.</p></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section id=\"software\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>5. Software</h2><p class=\"sub\">Programs and instructions that control or use computer hardware.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>System Software</h3><p>Manages hardware and provides a platform for applications.</p><span class=\"badge\">Operating System</span><span class=\"badge\">Drivers</span><span class=\"badge\">Utilities</span></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Application Software</h3><p>Performs tasks for users.</p><span class=\"badge green\">Browser</span><span class=\"badge green\">Word Processor</span><span class=\"badge green\">Media Player</span><span class=\"badge green\">Games</span></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Programming Software</h3><p>Tools used to create software: editors, compilers, interpreters and debuggers.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Compiler vs Interpreter</h3><p><b>Compiler:</b> translates a program before execution.</p><p><b>Interpreter:</b> executes program instructions through an interpreter at runtime.</p></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section id=\"os\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>6. Operating System</h2><p class=\"sub\">The OS manages resources and provides services to applications.</p>\n<div class=\"card\"><div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">Applications</div><div class=\"arrow\">↓</div><div class=\"box\">Operating System</div><div class=\"arrow\">↓</div><div class=\"box\">Hardware</div></div>\n<div class=\"grid\"><ul><li>Process management</li><li>Memory management</li><li>File management</li><li>Device management</li></ul><ul><li>Security</li><li>User interface</li><li>Resource allocation</li><li>Networking</li></ul></div></div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"io\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>7. Input & Output Devices</h2><p class=\"sub\">Devices used to communicate information with a computer.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Input</h3><p>Keyboard, mouse, scanner, microphone, webcam, touchscreen and barcode reader.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Output</h3><p>Monitor, printer, speakers, projector and headphones.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:14px\"><div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">Keyboard</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">CPU + Memory</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Monitor</div></div></div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"network\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>8. Computer Networking</h2><p class=\"sub\">Networks allow computers and devices to communicate and share resources.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Network Types</h3><p><span class=\"badge\">PAN</span> Personal Area Network</p><p><span class=\"badge\">LAN</span> Local Area Network</p><p><span class=\"badge\">MAN</span> Metropolitan Area Network</p><p><span class=\"badge\">WAN</span> Wide Area Network</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Network Devices</h3><ul><li><b>Switch:</b> connects devices in a network.</li><li><b>Router:</b> forwards traffic between networks.</li><li><b>Access Point:</b> provides wireless access.</li><li><b>Modem:</b> connects network equipment to a provider connection.</li></ul></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section id=\"internet\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>9. Internet Fundamentals</h2><p class=\"sub\">The Internet is a global network of interconnected networks.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>How a Website Loads</h3><div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">Browser</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">DNS</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Server</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Response</div></div><p>DNS resolves a domain name to an IP address so the client can locate the server.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Common Terms</h3><ul><li><b>IP:</b> network address.</li><li><b>Domain:</b> human-readable Internet name.</li><li><b>URL:</b> address of a web resource.</li><li><b>HTTP/HTTPS:</b> web communication protocols.</li></ul></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section id=\"security\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>10. Computer Security</h2><p class=\"sub\">Protect computers, data and users from unauthorized access and attacks.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>CIA Triad</h3><div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">Confidentiality</div><div class=\"box\">Integrity</div><div class=\"box\">Availability</div></div><p><b>Confidentiality:</b> authorized access only.</p><p><b>Integrity:</b> data remains accurate and unaltered.</p><p><b>Availability:</b> systems remain accessible when needed.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Common Threats</h3><ul><li>Malware</li><li>Phishing</li><li>Password attacks</li><li>Social engineering</li><li>Unauthorized access</li><li>Data theft</li></ul><div class=\"tip\"><b>Good practice:</b> strong unique passwords, MFA, updates, backups and careful link/file handling.</div></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section id=\"database\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>11. Database Fundamentals</h2><p class=\"sub\">Databases store, organize, query and update structured information.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Basic Model</h3><div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">Application</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">DBMS</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Database</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Relational Database</h3><p>Data is organized into tables made of rows and columns. SQL is commonly used to query relational databases.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Primary & Foreign Keys</h3><p><b>Primary key:</b> uniquely identifies a row.</p><p><b>Foreign key:</b> references a key in another table to represent a relationship.</p></div>\n<div class=\"card\"><h3>Example SQL</h3><pre>SELECT name, email\nFROM students\nWHERE active = 1\nORDER BY name;</pre></div>\n</div></section>\n\n\n<section id=\"detail\" class=\"reveal\">\n<h2>Detailed Revision Guide</h2>\n<p class=\"sub\">Expanded explanations for quick study, classroom learning and exam revision.</p>\n<div class=\"grid\">\n<article class=\"card\"><h3>Computer Characteristics</h3>\n<ul><li><b>Speed:</b> computers can perform large numbers of operations quickly.</li><li><b>Accuracy:</b> correct instructions and data can produce highly accurate results.</li><li><b>Automation:</b> once programmed, many tasks can run automatically.</li><li><b>Storage:</b> digital information can be stored and retrieved efficiently.</li><li><b>Versatility:</b> the same computer can perform many different tasks.</li></ul></article>\n<article class=\"card\"><h3>Generations of Computers</h3>\n<p><b>First generation:</b> vacuum tubes.</p><p><b>Second:</b> transistors.</p><p><b>Third:</b> integrated circuits.</p><p><b>Fourth:</b> microprocessors and personal computers.</p><p><b>Fifth:</b> commonly associated with advanced computing, AI and natural-language-oriented systems.</p></article>\n<article class=\"card\"><h3>Number Systems</h3>\n<table><tr><th>System</th><th>Base</th><th>Digits</th></tr><tr><td>Binary</td><td>2</td><td>0, 1</td></tr><tr><td>Octal</td><td>8</td><td>0–7</td></tr><tr><td>Decimal</td><td>10</td><td>0–9</td></tr><tr><td>Hexadecimal</td><td>16</td><td>0–9, A–F</td></tr></table>\n</article>\n<article class=\"card\"><h3>Units of Digital Storage</h3>\n<p><b>Bit:</b> smallest basic binary unit.</p><p><b>Byte:</b> commonly 8 bits.</p><p>Common larger units include KB, MB, GB and TB. Exact decimal vs binary conventions depend on context.</p></article>\n<article class=\"card\"><h3>Firmware & Drivers</h3>\n<p><b>Firmware</b> is software closely associated with hardware and stored in persistent memory.</p><p><b>Driver</b> software helps the operating system communicate with a hardware device.</p></article>\n<article class=\"card\"><h3>Booting</h3>\n<div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"box\">Power On</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Firmware</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">Bootloader</div><div class=\"arrow\">→</div><div class=\"box\">OS Kernel</div></div>\n<p>The boot process initializes hardware and loads the operating system.</p></article>\n<article class=\"card\"><h3>Cloud Computing</h3>\n<p>Cloud computing provides computing resources such as servers, storage and software services over networks. Common service models include IaaS, PaaS and SaaS.</p></article>\n<article class=\"card\"><h3>Backup vs Storage</h3>\n<p><b>Storage</b> keeps working data. <b>Backup</b> is a separate copy intended to help recover data after loss, corruption or accidental deletion.</p></article>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tip\"><b>Study method:</b> First understand the diagram, then learn the definition, then compare related concepts, and finally attempt the 50-question test without looking at the answers.</div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"quiz\" class=\"reveal\"><h2>12. 50-Question Computer Fundamentals Test</h2><p class=\"sub\">Four options per question · instant feedback · explanation · score tracking.</p><div class=\"quiz-tools\"><span id=\"quizScore\">Score: 0 / 50</span><button onclick=\"resetQuiz()\">Reset Quiz</button></div><div id=\"quizList\"></div></section><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"1\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>1. Which sequence represents the basic working cycle of a computer?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,1,0)\"><b>A.</b> Input → Process → Output</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,1,1)\"><b>B.</b> Output → Process → Input</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,1,2)\"><b>C.</b> Process → Input → Output</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,1,3)\"><b>D.</b> Input → Output → Process</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback1\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"2\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>2. Which unit is primarily responsible for executing program instructions?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,2,0)\"><b>A.</b> RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,2,1)\"><b>B.</b> CPU</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,2,2)\"><b>C.</b> Monitor</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,2,3)\"><b>D.</b> Keyboard</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback2\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"3\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>3. What does CPU stand for?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,3,0)\"><b>A.</b> Central Processing Unit</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,3,1)\"><b>B.</b> Computer Processing Utility</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,3,2)\"><b>C.</b> Central Program Unit</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,3,3)\"><b>D.</b> Core Processing User</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback3\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"4\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>4. Which component performs arithmetic and logical operations?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,4,0)\"><b>A.</b> Control Unit</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,4,1)\"><b>B.</b> ALU</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,4,2)\"><b>C.</b> RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,4,3)\"><b>D.</b> Power Supply</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback4\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"5\" data-answer=\"2\">\n<h3>5. What is the main function of the Control Unit?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,5,0)\"><b>A.</b> Store files permanently</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,5,1)\"><b>B.</b> Perform arithmetic only</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,5,2)\"><b>C.</b> Coordinate instruction execution</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,5,3)\"><b>D.</b> Display images</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback5\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"6\" data-answer=\"2\">\n<h3>6. Which is the fastest storage location among these?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,6,0)\"><b>A.</b> Hard disk</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,6,1)\"><b>B.</b> RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,6,2)\"><b>C.</b> CPU register</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,6,3)\"><b>D.</b> USB drive</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback6\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"7\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>7. Which memory is normally volatile?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,7,0)\"><b>A.</b> ROM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,7,1)\"><b>B.</b> RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,7,2)\"><b>C.</b> SSD</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,7,3)\"><b>D.</b> DVD</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback7\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"8\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>8. What is the main purpose of RAM?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,8,0)\"><b>A.</b> Permanent file storage</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,8,1)\"><b>B.</b> Temporary working storage for active programs</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,8,2)\"><b>C.</b> Printing documents</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,8,3)\"><b>D.</b> Connecting networks</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback8\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"9\" data-answer=\"3\">\n<h3>9. Which storage device normally retains data after power is removed?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,9,0)\"><b>A.</b> RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,9,1)\"><b>B.</b> Cache</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,9,2)\"><b>C.</b> Register</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,9,3)\"><b>D.</b> SSD</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback9\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"10\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>10. What is cache memory used for?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,10,0)\"><b>A.</b> Long-term backup</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,10,1)\"><b>B.</b> Speeding access to frequently used data/instructions</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,10,2)\"><b>C.</b> Printing</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,10,3)\"><b>D.</b> Network routing</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback10\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"11\" data-answer=\"2\">\n<h3>11. Which device is an input device?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,11,0)\"><b>A.</b> Monitor</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,11,1)\"><b>B.</b> Printer</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,11,2)\"><b>C.</b> Keyboard</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,11,3)\"><b>D.</b> Speaker</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback11\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"12\" data-answer=\"3\">\n<h3>12. Which device is an output device?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,12,0)\"><b>A.</b> Mouse</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,12,1)\"><b>B.</b> Scanner</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,12,2)\"><b>C.</b> Microphone</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,12,3)\"><b>D.</b> Monitor</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback12\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"13\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>13. What is a motherboard?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,13,0)\"><b>A.</b> A software program</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,13,1)\"><b>B.</b> The main circuit board connecting computer components</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,13,2)\"><b>C.</b> A storage file</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,13,3)\"><b>D.</b> A network protocol</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback13\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"14\" data-answer=\"2\">\n<h3>14. Which component is commonly used for long-term data storage?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,14,0)\"><b>A.</b> RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,14,1)\"><b>B.</b> CPU register</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,14,2)\"><b>C.</b> SSD</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,14,3)\"><b>D.</b> Cache</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback14\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"15\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>15. What is hardware?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,15,0)\"><b>A.</b> Physical computer components</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,15,1)\"><b>B.</b> Only operating systems</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,15,2)\"><b>C.</b> Only applications</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,15,3)\"><b>D.</b> Internet data</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback15\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"16\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>16. What is software?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,16,0)\"><b>A.</b> Physical circuitry</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,16,1)\"><b>B.</b> Programs and instructions</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,16,2)\"><b>C.</b> Only cables</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,16,3)\"><b>D.</b> A power source</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback16\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"17\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>17. Which is an example of system software?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,17,0)\"><b>A.</b> Operating system</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,17,1)\"><b>B.</b> Photo</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,17,2)\"><b>C.</b> Music file</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,17,3)\"><b>D.</b> Spreadsheet document</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback17\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"18\" data-answer=\"2\">\n<h3>18. Which is an example of application software?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,18,0)\"><b>A.</b> Device driver</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,18,1)\"><b>B.</b> Operating system</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,18,2)\"><b>C.</b> Web browser</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,18,3)\"><b>D.</b> Boot firmware</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback18\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"19\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>19. What does a compiler generally do?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,19,0)\"><b>A.</b> Translates source code before execution</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,19,1)\"><b>B.</b> Prints source code</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,19,2)\"><b>C.</b> Stores files</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,19,3)\"><b>D.</b> Connects Wi-Fi</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback19\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"20\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>20. What does an interpreter generally do?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,20,0)\"><b>A.</b> Physically repairs hardware</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,20,1)\"><b>B.</b> Executes/translates program instructions at runtime</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,20,2)\"><b>C.</b> Provides electrical power</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,20,3)\"><b>D.</b> Formats a monitor</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback20\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"21\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>21. What is the main role of an operating system?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,21,0)\"><b>A.</b> Manage resources and provide services to programs</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,21,1)\"><b>B.</b> Only browse the Internet</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,21,2)\"><b>C.</b> Only edit images</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,21,3)\"><b>D.</b> Only store music</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback21\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"22\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>22. Which is an operating system function?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,22,0)\"><b>A.</b> Process management</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,22,1)\"><b>B.</b> Screen cleaning</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,22,2)\"><b>C.</b> Keyboard manufacturing</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,22,3)\"><b>D.</b> Cable production</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback22\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"23\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>23. What is a process?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,23,0)\"><b>A.</b> A program in execution</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,23,1)\"><b>B.</b> A keyboard key</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,23,2)\"><b>C.</b> A storage cable</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,23,3)\"><b>D.</b> A network port</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback23\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"24\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>24. What does GUI stand for?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,24,0)\"><b>A.</b> Graphical User Interface</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,24,1)\"><b>B.</b> General Utility Input</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,24,2)\"><b>C.</b> Global User Internet</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,24,3)\"><b>D.</b> Graphic Unit Instruction</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback24\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"25\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>25. What does CLI stand for?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,25,0)\"><b>A.</b> Command Line Interface</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,25,1)\"><b>B.</b> Computer Logic Input</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,25,2)\"><b>C.</b> Central Link Internet</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,25,3)\"><b>D.</b> Control Language Instruction</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback25\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"26\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>26. What does I/O mean?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,26,0)\"><b>A.</b> Input/Output</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,26,1)\"><b>B.</b> Internet/Online</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,26,2)\"><b>C.</b> Internal/Operating</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,26,3)\"><b>D.</b> Instruction/Order</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback26\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"27\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>27. Which is an input device used to capture sound?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,27,0)\"><b>A.</b> Speaker</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,27,1)\"><b>B.</b> Microphone</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,27,2)\"><b>C.</b> Monitor</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,27,3)\"><b>D.</b> Projector</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback27\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"28\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>28. Which device produces printed output?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,28,0)\"><b>A.</b> Scanner</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,28,1)\"><b>B.</b> Printer</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,28,2)\"><b>C.</b> Keyboard</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,28,3)\"><b>D.</b> Mouse</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback28\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"29\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>29. What is a computer network?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,29,0)\"><b>A.</b> A group of connected devices that communicate</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,29,1)\"><b>B.</b> A single CPU</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,29,2)\"><b>C.</b> A type of RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,29,3)\"><b>D.</b> A text editor</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback29\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"30\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>30. What does LAN stand for?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,30,0)\"><b>A.</b> Local Area Network</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,30,1)\"><b>B.</b> Large Access Node</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,30,2)\"><b>C.</b> Logical Area Number</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,30,3)\"><b>D.</b> Local Application Network</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback30\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"31\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>31. What does WAN stand for?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,31,0)\"><b>A.</b> Wide Area Network</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,31,1)\"><b>B.</b> Wireless Application Node</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,31,2)\"><b>C.</b> Web Access Network</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,31,3)\"><b>D.</b> Wide Application Number</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback31\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"32\" data-answer=\"1\">\n<h3>32. Which device forwards packets between different networks?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,32,0)\"><b>A.</b> Switch</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,32,1)\"><b>B.</b> Router</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,32,2)\"><b>C.</b> Keyboard</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,32,3)\"><b>D.</b> Printer</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback32\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"33\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>33. What is the main role of a network switch?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,33,0)\"><b>A.</b> Connect devices within a network</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,33,1)\"><b>B.</b> Execute CPU instructions</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,33,2)\"><b>C.</b> Store operating systems</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,33,3)\"><b>D.</b> Print documents</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback33\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"34\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>34. What does an IP address identify?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,34,0)\"><b>A.</b> A network interface/device address</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,34,1)\"><b>B.</b> A file extension</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,34,2)\"><b>C.</b> A CPU instruction</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,34,3)\"><b>D.</b> A keyboard layout</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback34\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"35\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>35. What does DNS primarily do?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,35,0)\"><b>A.</b> Translate domain names to IP addresses</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,35,1)\"><b>B.</b> Encrypt every file</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,35,2)\"><b>C.</b> Create RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,35,3)\"><b>D.</b> Print web pages</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback35\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"36\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>36. What does URL stand for?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,36,0)\"><b>A.</b> Uniform Resource Locator</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,36,1)\"><b>B.</b> Universal Router Link</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,36,2)\"><b>C.</b> User Resource Language</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,36,3)\"><b>D.</b> Unified Runtime Location</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback36\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"37\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>37. What is HTTPS?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,37,0)\"><b>A.</b> A secure version of HTTP using encryption mechanisms</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,37,1)\"><b>B.</b> A type of RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,37,2)\"><b>C.</b> A CPU instruction</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,37,3)\"><b>D.</b> A database table</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback37\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"38\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>38. Which protocol is commonly used to transfer web pages?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,38,0)\"><b>A.</b> HTTP</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,38,1)\"><b>B.</b> RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,38,2)\"><b>C.</b> CPU</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,38,3)\"><b>D.</b> BIOS</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback38\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"39\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>39. What is malware?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,39,0)\"><b>A.</b> Malicious software</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,39,1)\"><b>B.</b> Memory hardware</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,39,2)\"><b>C.</b> A network cable</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,39,3)\"><b>D.</b> A database key</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback39\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"40\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>40. What is phishing?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,40,0)\"><b>A.</b> A deceptive attempt to obtain information by pretending to be trustworthy</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,40,1)\"><b>B.</b> A disk scheduling method</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,40,2)\"><b>C.</b> A CPU operation</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,40,3)\"><b>D.</b> A type of RAM</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback40\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"41\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>41. What does MFA provide?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,41,0)\"><b>A.</b> An additional authentication factor beyond a single credential</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,41,1)\"><b>B.</b> More RAM</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,41,2)\"><b>C.</b> Faster CPU execution</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,41,3)\"><b>D.</b> Automatic backups only</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback41\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"42\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>42. What does confidentiality mean in the CIA triad?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,42,0)\"><b>A.</b> Authorized parties can access information</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,42,1)\"><b>B.</b> Data is always available</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,42,2)\"><b>C.</b> Data is compressed</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,42,3)\"><b>D.</b> CPU is fast</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback42\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"43\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>43. What does integrity mean in cybersecurity?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,43,0)\"><b>A.</b> Information remains accurate and unaltered improperly</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,43,1)\"><b>B.</b> Every system is online</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,43,2)\"><b>C.</b> Files are always compressed</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,43,3)\"><b>D.</b> Passwords are public</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback43\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"44\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>44. What does availability mean?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,44,0)\"><b>A.</b> Systems and information are accessible when needed</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,44,1)\"><b>B.</b> Only administrators can use a system</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,44,2)\"><b>C.</b> Data is always encrypted</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,44,3)\"><b>D.</b> A CPU never stops</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback44\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"45\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>45. What is a database?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,45,0)\"><b>A.</b> An organized collection of data</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,45,1)\"><b>B.</b> A computer monitor</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,45,2)\"><b>C.</b> A CPU register</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,45,3)\"><b>D.</b> A network cable</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback45\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"46\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>46. What does DBMS stand for?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,46,0)\"><b>A.</b> Database Management System</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,46,1)\"><b>B.</b> Data Backup Memory Service</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,46,2)\"><b>C.</b> Digital Binary Management Software</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,46,3)\"><b>D.</b> Database Machine Storage</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback46\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"47\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>47. What is a primary key?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,47,0)\"><b>A.</b> A column or set of columns that uniquely identifies a row</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,47,1)\"><b>B.</b> A password for the computer</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,47,2)\"><b>C.</b> A network cable</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,47,3)\"><b>D.</b> A file extension</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback47\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"48\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>48. What is a foreign key?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,48,0)\"><b>A.</b> A field that references a key in another table</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,48,1)\"><b>B.</b> A CPU register</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,48,2)\"><b>C.</b> A type of monitor</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,48,3)\"><b>D.</b> A network address</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback48\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"49\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>49. Which SQL command retrieves data?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,49,0)\"><b>A.</b> SELECT</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,49,1)\"><b>B.</b> DELETE</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,49,2)\"><b>C.</b> CREATE</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,49,3)\"><b>D.</b> DROP</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback49\"></div></article><article class=\"card quiz-card\" data-question=\"50\" data-answer=\"0\">\n<h3>50. Which is a good basic security practice?</h3><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,50,0)\"><b>A.</b> Use strong unique passwords and MFA</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,50,1)\"><b>B.</b> Share passwords publicly</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,50,2)\"><b>C.</b> Disable all updates</button><button class=\"quiz-option\" onclick=\"answerQuestion(this,50,3)\"><b>D.</b> Open unknown attachments</button><div class=\"quiz-feedback\" id=\"feedback50\"></div></article>\n</main>\n\n<footer>Computer Fundamentals · Lightweight Interactive HTML Notes · Works Offline</footer>\n\n<script>\nconst questions=[\n[\"What is the basic computer cycle?\",[\"Input → Process → Output\",\"Output → Input → Process\",\"Process → Output → Input\",\"Storage → Output → Input\"],0],\n[\"Which component executes instructions?\",[\"Monitor\",\"CPU\",\"Keyboard\",\"Printer\"],1],\n[\"Which memory is normally volatile?\",[\"RAM\",\"SSD\",\"ROM\",\"Optical disc\"],0],\n[\"What does an operating system manage?\",[\"Only documents\",\"Only websites\",\"Hardware and system resources\",\"Only keyboards\"],2],\n[\"Which device forwards traffic between networks?\",[\"Router\",\"Keyboard\",\"Monitor\",\"Scanner\"],0],\n[\"What does DNS primarily do?\",[\"Compress files\",\"Translate domain names to IP addresses\",\"Create passwords\",\"Print documents\"],1],\n[\"Which is part of the CIA security triad?\",[\"Caching\",\"Confidentiality\",\"Compilation\",\"Calculation\"],1],\n[\"Which key uniquely identifies a relational table row?\",[\"Primary key\",\"CSS key\",\"Network key\",\"Display key\"],0]\n];\ndocument.getElementById(\"quiz\").innerHTML=questions.map((q,i)=>`\n<div class=\"card quiz\"><h3>${i+1}. ${q[0]}</h3>\n${q[1].map((x,j)=>`<button onclick=\"check(this,${i},${j})\">${x}</button>`).join(\"\")}\n<div class=\"result\" id=\"r${i}\"></div></div>`).join(\"\");\nfunction check(btn,i,j){\n const box=btn.parentElement;if(box.dataset.done)return;box.dataset.done=\"1\";\n if(j===questions[i][2]){btn.style.background=\"#dcfce7\";btn.style.borderColor=\"#86efac\";document.getElementById(\"r\"+i).textContent=\"Correct ✓\";}\n else{btn.style.background=\"#fee2e2\";btn.style.borderColor=\"#fca5a5\";document.getElementById(\"r\"+i).textContent=\"Correct answer: \"+questions[i][1][questions[i][2]];}\n}\nconst observer=new IntersectionObserver(es=>es.forEach(e=>{if(e.isIntersecting)e.target.classList.add(\"show\")}),{threshold:.08});\ndocument.querySelectorAll(\".reveal\").forEach(x=>observer.observe(x));\n\nlet quizCorrect=0,quizAnswered=0;\nfunction answerQuestion(btn,num,index){\n  const card=btn.closest(\'.quiz-card\');\n  if(card.dataset.done)return;\n  card.dataset.done=\"1\";quizAnswered++;\n  const answer=Number(card.dataset.answer);\n  const buttons=[...card.querySelectorAll(\'.quiz-option\')];\n  buttons[answer].classList.add(\'correct\');\n  const feedback=document.getElementById(\'feedback\'+num);\n  if(index===answer){\n    quizCorrect++;\n    feedback.textContent=\'✓ Correct! \'+questions50[num-1][3];\n  }else{\n    btn.classList.add(\'wrong\');\n    feedback.textContent=\'Correct answer: \'+String.fromCharCode(65+answer)+\'. \'+questions50[num-1][1][answer]+\' — \'+questions50[num-1][3];\n  }\n  document.getElementById(\'quizScore\').textContent=\'Score: \'+quizCorrect+\' / 50 · Answered: \'+quizAnswered+\' / 50\';\n}\nfunction resetQuiz(){\n  quizCorrect=0;quizAnswered=0;\n  document.getElementById(\'quizScore\').textContent=\'Score: 0 / 50\';\n  document.querySelectorAll(\'.quiz-card\').forEach(card=>{\n    delete card.dataset.done;\n    card.querySelectorAll(\'.quiz-option\').forEach(b=>b.classList.remove(\'correct\',\'wrong\'));\n    card.querySelector(\'.quiz-feedback\').textContent=\'\';\n  });\n}\nconst questions50=[[\"Which sequence represents the basic working cycle of a computer?\", [\"Input → Process → Output\", \"Output → Process → Input\", \"Process → Input → Output\", \"Input → Output → Process\"], 0, \"A computer generally accepts input, processes it, and produces output.\"], [\"Which unit is primarily responsible for executing program instructions?\", [\"RAM\", \"CPU\", \"Monitor\", \"Keyboard\"], 1, \"The CPU executes instructions and performs calculations and control operations.\"], [\"What does CPU stand for?\", [\"Central Processing Unit\", \"Computer Processing Utility\", \"Central Program Unit\", \"Core Processing User\"], 0, \"CPU means Central Processing Unit.\"], [\"Which component performs arithmetic and logical operations?\", [\"Control Unit\", \"ALU\", \"RAM\", \"Power Supply\"], 1, \"The Arithmetic Logic Unit performs arithmetic and logical operations.\"], [\"What is the main function of the Control Unit?\", [\"Store files permanently\", \"Perform arithmetic only\", \"Coordinate instruction execution\", \"Display images\"], 2, \"The Control Unit coordinates and directs CPU operations.\"], [\"Which is the fastest storage location among these?\", [\"Hard disk\", \"RAM\", \"CPU register\", \"USB drive\"], 2, \"CPU registers are extremely small and very fast storage locations inside the processor.\"], [\"Which memory is normally volatile?\", [\"ROM\", \"RAM\", \"SSD\", \"DVD\"], 1, \"RAM loses its stored contents when power is removed.\"], [\"What is the main purpose of RAM?\", [\"Permanent file storage\", \"Temporary working storage for active programs\", \"Printing documents\", \"Connecting networks\"], 1, \"RAM holds programs and data currently being used by the system.\"], [\"Which storage device normally retains data after power is removed?\", [\"RAM\", \"Cache\", \"Register\", \"SSD\"], 3, \"SSD is non-volatile secondary storage.\"], [\"What is cache memory used for?\", [\"Long-term backup\", \"Speeding access to frequently used data/instructions\", \"Printing\", \"Network routing\"], 1, \"Cache stores frequently or recently used information close to the CPU for faster access.\"], [\"Which device is an input device?\", [\"Monitor\", \"Printer\", \"Keyboard\", \"Speaker\"], 2, \"A keyboard sends data and commands into the computer.\"], [\"Which device is an output device?\", [\"Mouse\", \"Scanner\", \"Microphone\", \"Monitor\"], 3, \"A monitor displays processed information to the user.\"], [\"What is a motherboard?\", [\"A software program\", \"The main circuit board connecting computer components\", \"A storage file\", \"A network protocol\"], 1, \"The motherboard connects major components and provides communication pathways.\"], [\"Which component is commonly used for long-term data storage?\", [\"RAM\", \"CPU register\", \"SSD\", \"Cache\"], 2, \"An SSD provides persistent storage.\"], [\"What is hardware?\", [\"Physical computer components\", \"Only operating systems\", \"Only applications\", \"Internet data\"], 0, \"Hardware refers to physical components that can be physically handled.\"], [\"What is software?\", [\"Physical circuitry\", \"Programs and instructions\", \"Only cables\", \"A power source\"], 1, \"Software consists of programs and instructions executed by a computer.\"], [\"Which is an example of system software?\", [\"Operating system\", \"Photo\", \"Music file\", \"Spreadsheet document\"], 0, \"An operating system is system software that manages hardware and provides services.\"], [\"Which is an example of application software?\", [\"Device driver\", \"Operating system\", \"Web browser\", \"Boot firmware\"], 2, \"A web browser is application software used for a user task.\"], [\"What does a compiler generally do?\", [\"Translates source code before execution\", \"Prints source code\", \"Stores files\", \"Connects Wi-Fi\"], 0, \"A compiler translates source code into another form before execution.\"], [\"What does an interpreter generally do?\", [\"Physically repairs hardware\", \"Executes/translates program instructions at runtime\", \"Provides electrical power\", \"Formats a monitor\"], 1, \"An interpreter processes program instructions during execution.\"], [\"What is the main role of an operating system?\", [\"Manage resources and provide services to programs\", \"Only browse the Internet\", \"Only edit images\", \"Only store music\"], 0, \"The OS manages CPU, memory, files, devices, security and other resources.\"], [\"Which is an operating system function?\", [\"Process management\", \"Screen cleaning\", \"Keyboard manufacturing\", \"Cable production\"], 0, \"Process management is a core OS responsibility.\"], [\"What is a process?\", [\"A program in execution\", \"A keyboard key\", \"A storage cable\", \"A network port\"], 0, \"A process is a running instance of a program.\"], [\"What does GUI stand for?\", [\"Graphical User Interface\", \"General Utility Input\", \"Global User Internet\", \"Graphic Unit Instruction\"], 0, \"GUI means Graphical User Interface.\"], [\"What does CLI stand for?\", [\"Command Line Interface\", \"Computer Logic Input\", \"Central Link Internet\", \"Control Language Instruction\"], 0, \"CLI means Command Line Interface.\"], [\"What does I/O mean?\", [\"Input/Output\", \"Internet/Online\", \"Internal/Operating\", \"Instruction/Order\"], 0, \"I/O stands for Input/Output.\"], [\"Which is an input device used to capture sound?\", [\"Speaker\", \"Microphone\", \"Monitor\", \"Projector\"], 1, \"A microphone captures audio as input.\"], [\"Which device produces printed output?\", [\"Scanner\", \"Printer\", \"Keyboard\", \"Mouse\"], 1, \"A printer produces physical printed output.\"], [\"What is a computer network?\", [\"A group of connected devices that communicate\", \"A single CPU\", \"A type of RAM\", \"A text editor\"], 0, \"A network connects devices so they can exchange data and share resources.\"], [\"What does LAN stand for?\", [\"Local Area Network\", \"Large Access Node\", \"Logical Area Number\", \"Local Application Network\"], 0, \"LAN means Local Area Network.\"], [\"What does WAN stand for?\", [\"Wide Area Network\", \"Wireless Application Node\", \"Web Access Network\", \"Wide Application Number\"], 0, \"WAN means Wide Area Network.\"], [\"Which device forwards packets between different networks?\", [\"Switch\", \"Router\", \"Keyboard\", \"Printer\"], 1, \"A router forwards traffic between networks.\"], [\"What is the main role of a network switch?\", [\"Connect devices within a network\", \"Execute CPU instructions\", \"Store operating systems\", \"Print documents\"], 0, \"A switch connects devices and forwards traffic within a local network.\"], [\"What does an IP address identify?\", [\"A network interface/device address\", \"A file extension\", \"A CPU instruction\", \"A keyboard layout\"], 0, \"An IP address identifies a network interface for communication.\"], [\"What does DNS primarily do?\", [\"Translate domain names to IP addresses\", \"Encrypt every file\", \"Create RAM\", \"Print web pages\"], 0, \"DNS resolves human-readable domain names to IP addresses.\"], [\"What does URL stand for?\", [\"Uniform Resource Locator\", \"Universal Router Link\", \"User Resource Language\", \"Unified Runtime Location\"], 0, \"URL means Uniform Resource Locator.\"], [\"What is HTTPS?\", [\"A secure version of HTTP using encryption mechanisms\", \"A type of RAM\", \"A CPU instruction\", \"A database table\"], 0, \"HTTPS protects web communication using TLS encryption.\"], [\"Which protocol is commonly used to transfer web pages?\", [\"HTTP\", \"RAM\", \"CPU\", \"BIOS\"], 0, \"HTTP is a protocol used for web communication.\"], [\"What is malware?\", [\"Malicious software\", \"Memory hardware\", \"A network cable\", \"A database key\"], 0, \"Malware is software designed to harm, disrupt, spy on, or gain unauthorized access to systems.\"], [\"What is phishing?\", [\"A deceptive attempt to obtain information by pretending to be trustworthy\", \"A disk scheduling method\", \"A CPU operation\", \"A type of RAM\"], 0, \"Phishing commonly uses deceptive messages or sites to trick people into revealing information.\"], [\"What does MFA provide?\", [\"An additional authentication factor beyond a single credential\", \"More RAM\", \"Faster CPU execution\", \"Automatic backups only\"], 0, \"Multi-factor authentication requires multiple forms of evidence to verify identity.\"], [\"What does confidentiality mean in the CIA triad?\", [\"Authorized parties can access information\", \"Data is always available\", \"Data is compressed\", \"CPU is fast\"], 0, \"Confidentiality focuses on preventing unauthorized access to information.\"], [\"What does integrity mean in cybersecurity?\", [\"Information remains accurate and unaltered improperly\", \"Every system is online\", \"Files are always compressed\", \"Passwords are public\"], 0, \"Integrity protects information from unauthorized or unintended modification.\"], [\"What does availability mean?\", [\"Systems and information are accessible when needed\", \"Only administrators can use a system\", \"Data is always encrypted\", \"A CPU never stops\"], 0, \"Availability focuses on reliable access to systems and information.\"], [\"What is a database?\", [\"An organized collection of data\", \"A computer monitor\", \"A CPU register\", \"A network cable\"], 0, \"A database organizes data so it can be stored, queried and updated.\"], [\"What does DBMS stand for?\", [\"Database Management System\", \"Data Backup Memory Service\", \"Digital Binary Management Software\", \"Database Machine Storage\"], 0, \"DBMS means Database Management System.\"], [\"What is a primary key?\", [\"A column or set of columns that uniquely identifies a row\", \"A password for the computer\", \"A network cable\", \"A file extension\"], 0, \"A primary key uniquely identifies records in a relational table.\"], [\"What is a foreign key?\", [\"A field that references a key in another table\", \"A CPU register\", \"A type of monitor\", \"A network address\"], 0, \"A foreign key represents a relationship by referencing a key in another table.\"], [\"Which SQL command retrieves data?\", [\"SELECT\", \"DELETE\", \"CREATE\", \"DROP\"], 0, \"SELECT is used to query and retrieve data from tables.\"], [\"Which is a good basic security practice?\", [\"Use strong unique passwords and MFA\", \"Share passwords publicly\", \"Disable all updates\", \"Open unknown attachments\"], 0, \"Strong unique passwords, MFA, updates and cautious handling of links/files improve security.\"]];\n\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>',1,0.00,0.00,0.00,NULL,'SELECTED_CENTRES','BOTH',NULL,'PUBLISHED',NULL,1,'center',1,0,4,'2026-10-04 14:54:16','2026-10-04 16:00:18',20.00),(20,'DTFYU','dtfyu-108','Programming','ejrbgij',NULL,'','HTML','2.5 MB','<h1>hello</h1>',1,0.00,0.00,0.00,NULL,'SELECTED_CENTRES','BOTH',NULL,'PUBLISHED',NULL,1,'center',1,0,4,'2026-10-04 15:16:05','2026-10-04 15:57:18',20.00),(21,'sfdth','sfdth-333','Science','hbedfhb',NULL,'/uploads/branding/img-1791127641797-869.pdf','PDF','0.9 MB','',1,0.00,0.00,0.00,NULL,'SELECTED_CENTRES','BOTH',NULL,'PUBLISHED',NULL,1,'center',1,0,2,'2026-10-04 15:27:21','2026-10-04 15:57:12',20.00),(22,'b fdsfbd','b-fdsfbd-9','English','dfb df','/uploads/branding/img-1791910440317-793.png','/uploads/branding/img-1791127671727-169.pdf','PDF','7.2 MB','',1,0.00,0.00,0.00,NULL,'SELECTED_CENTRES','BOTH',NULL,'PENDING_APPROVAL',NULL,1,'center',1,0,0,'2026-10-04 15:27:51','2026-10-13 16:54:09',20.00);
